{"id":3560,"date":"2017-07-18T16:32:49","date_gmt":"2017-07-18T21:32:49","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/pokernight.com\/poker-night-in-america-signs-new-title-sponsor-kimo-sabe-mezcal-2-2\/"},"modified":"2017-07-20T11:58:49","modified_gmt":"2017-07-20T16:58:49","slug":"sitngobecomesfeaturedsponsor","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/pokernight.com\/sitngobecomesfeaturedsponsor\/","title":{"rendered":"SIT &#038; GO 2.0 Becomes Featured Sponsor of National TV&#8217;s Poker Night In America"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>[et_pb_section fb_built=&#8221;1&#8243; background_color=&#8221;#f2f2f2&#8243; custom_padding=&#8221;|0px||0px&#8221; admin_label=&#8221;section&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;3.0.47&#8243;][et_pb_row make_fullwidth=&#8221;on&#8221; use_custom_gutter=&#8221;on&#8221; gutter_width=&#8221;1&#8243; background_color=&#8221;#f2f2f2&#8243; parallax_method_1=&#8221;off&#8221; admin_label=&#8221;row&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;3.0.47&#8243; background_size=&#8221;initial&#8221; background_position=&#8221;top_left&#8221; background_repeat=&#8221;repeat&#8221;][et_pb_column type=&#8221;4_4&#8243; _builder_version=&#8221;3.0.47&#8243; parallax=&#8221;off&#8221; parallax_method=&#8221;off&#8221;][et_pb_text _builder_version=&#8221;3.0.62&#8243; background_color=&#8221;#f2f2f2&#8243; background_size=&#8221;initial&#8221; background_position=&#8221;top_left&#8221; background_repeat=&#8221;repeat&#8221; custom_margin=&#8221;||50px|&#8221;]<\/p>\n<h2><b><i>The Hit TV Series Teams Up With Industry Innovators To Bring The Next Evolution in Tournament Poker <\/i><\/b><\/h2>\n<p><b>Chicago, Illinois \u2013 July 17, 2017 \u2013<\/b> <a href=\"https:\/\/pokernight.com\/\"><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Poker Night in America<\/span><\/i><\/a><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, <\/span><\/i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">the high stakes poker series that airs every Monday &amp; Sunday on CBS Sports Network, is adding a new sponsor to their Featured Partner roster with Sit &amp; Go 2.0, the revolutionary new prize pool system for live and online Sit &amp; Go Tournaments.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This innovative format is injecting an exciting new concept to the traditional sit-and-go. The rules in poker gameplay for Sit &amp; Go 2.0 are exactly the same as a standard sit &amp; go, but what makes it unique is the prize pool modification that happens before the cards are shuffled-up and dealt.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The game begins with the dealer dealing out 9 cards, face down around the table. \u00a0The player to the left of the dealer button then begins by revealing their card. \u00a0A red card means stop, and a black card means go. \u00a0If a red card is shown, the prize pool stays the same as outlined during registration. \u00a0The cards are then shuffled and the regular sit-and-go resumes. \u00a0However, if the player reveals a black card, the prize pool increases and the next player reveals their card. \u00a0With each black card that is revealed, the prize pool and number of players paid increases significantly. \u00a0The prize pool keeps increasing until a red card is revealed. \u00a0Unlike a regular sit-and-go, where there\u2019s a set prize pool for every game, the prize pool for 2.0 games have yet to be determined, adding an element of chance to each game!<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u201cThis new sponsorship is a perfect fit for us,\u201d said Todd Anderson, President at Rush Street Productions, the company behind <\/span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Poker Night<\/span><\/i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. \u00a0\u201cWe exist to make traditional poker fun again, and Sit &amp; Go 2.0 has just reinvigorated a traditional form of the game, so our goals of our two companies are perfectly aligned &#8211; to make poker more fun and accessible.\u201d<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Sit &amp; Go 2.0\u2019s branding will begin to appear in nationally-broadcast episodes of <\/span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Poker Night in America<\/span><\/i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> starting in early August, and will include prominent placement of their logo in-show, on Poker Night\u2019s social media pages, on <\/span><a href=\"http:\/\/www.twitch.tv\/PokerNightTV\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Twitch livestreams<\/span><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, and will also include commercial runs during the breaks. \u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p><b>About Poker Night in America <\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Founded in 2013, Rush Street Productions brought America\u2019s true pastime, Texas Hold\u2019em Poker, to television screens nationwide on CBS Sports Network with its hit series Poker Night in America. \u00a0Currently in its fifth season, and with \u00a0more than 150 episodes produced, Poker Night in America continues to showcase amazing cash game poker each week played by the game\u2019s best players and celebrities. It also pioneers in the emerging market of live poker streaming. \u00a0For more information, visit pokernight.com or follow Poker Night on Twitter, Youtube, and Twitch.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Media Contact:<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Todd Anderson<\/span><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"mailto:pokernightinamerica@gmail.com\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">pokernightinamerica@gmail.com<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n<p>[\/et_pb_text][et_pb_video src=&#8221;https:\/\/youtu.be\/jnivtQ7QlHo&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;3.0.62&#8243;][\/et_pb_video][\/et_pb_column][\/et_pb_row][\/et_pb_section]<\/p>\n<span class=\"et_bloom_bottom_trigger\"><\/span>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>The Hit TV Series Teams Up With Industry Innovators To Bring The Next Evolution in Tournament Poker &#8211; Chicago, Illinois \u2013 July 17, 2017 \u2013 Poker Night in America, the high&#8230;<\/p>\n","